WEBVTT

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:21.270
Anehara Cross School of Magic

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:23.660
I want to change!

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:26.990
I might be able to change. That's why I...

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:16.710
Did you need something?

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:24.690
A school for mages.

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:27.450
I'm not sure where you heard that,
but my rate is pretty high.

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:27.430
A school that teaches you magic.

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:31.920
That's what was written on the
pamphlet I found, but...

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:31.600
If you take a normal student's

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:34.010
allowance for the month,
it'd probably be 300 times that.

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:36.290
Is it really that expensive?

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:39.010
She thinks this is a school for magic.

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:42.100
Oh, yeah. This is my great-grandfather's Code.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:43.940
Let's see... What's your name?

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:45.650
Morishita Koyomi.

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:51.600
Sorry to say it, but this was only a school back in the 1800s and early 1900s.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:53.620
Now, it's just a normal residence.

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:55.300
No way...

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:58.730
This is pretty impressive, though.

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:01.590
A ton of spells are in the paper's watermark.

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:09.410
It's just a magic trick.

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:11.240
She said "spells" just now.

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:15.670
Why are there always crazy people like this girl asking my sister for things?

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:17.350
There's no way magic exists.

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:23.160
You can't just call one of my business partners crazy right in front of them. Pout! Pout!

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:25.150
You can't use "pout" that way!

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:27.720
And besides, how long are you going to stay dressed like that?

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:30.560
What's wrong with my shirt?

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:33.160
And what's with this weird letter, anyway?

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:34.900
"If you want to change yourself..."

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:36.180
"Anyone can do it!"

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:38.100
Sounds like someone out for your money!

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:41.310
O-Out for my money? Th-That's not good.

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:44.690
I don't get much allowance...

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:49.370
You're fun.

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:54.530
Come with me. I'll show you something good.

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:12.580
This is...

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:17.510
Where I work.

00:04:17.510 --> 00:04:20.940
I guess you could call it a sorceress's studio.

00:04:30.110 --> 00:04:32.590
A sorceress's studio...

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:36.180
Anyway, take them off.

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:38.040
Take them off...

00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:50.690
Okay, stand on that.

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:57.100
Wh-What's going on?! It tingles!

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.740
Oh, you can tell?

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:00.580
That's a Code.

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:02.970
What's a Code?

00:05:02.970 --> 00:05:06.530
To put it simply, it's the source of all magic.

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:11.200
There's a Code circulating in this,

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.820
but you can't make magic with that alone.

00:05:13.820 --> 00:05:16.290
You could say it's 99% done.

00:05:17.570 --> 00:05:20.790
That's why you're the remaining 1%.

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:21.570
But-

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:25.440
It's okay. All you have to do is concentrate.

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:27.060
What about saying spells?

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.320
There aren't any.

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:32.230
Those are just something to help you focus.

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:36.910
If you really wanted to, you could think of the guy you like or something.

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:38.380
I don't like anyone right now.

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:41.750
It doesn't matter what it is, as long as you concentrate.

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:46.170
And if nothing unusual happens, everything will go fine.

00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:48.200
Nothing dangerous to worry about, either.

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:50.550
Relax.

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:55.360
Okay, let's start.

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:58.330
Focus on where you're stepping.

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:03.250
Concentrate. Concentrate.

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:14.510
No! A mean guy like that isn't anything to me!

00:06:14.510 --> 00:06:17.000
Oh, yeah! If I end up able to use magic,

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:19.600
I can really give it to him!

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:25.020
What is this?

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:28.640
It feels like a mix of cold and heat spinning inside me.

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:30.780
Is this magic?

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:39.280
That's weird. I was certain the Code-

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:41.750
Get down!

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.660
Wh-What are...

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:47.990
You can see them?

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:49.900
What are those?

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:52.040
You can see the Daemons clearly?

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:55.050
Watch out!

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:04.860
Keep your head down.

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:12.070
Watch out!

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:35.590
Are you okay? You're not hurt?

00:07:35.590 --> 00:07:37.100
I-I'm okay.

00:07:39.710 --> 00:07:44.490
I wonder how they got in here...

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:48.940
Um, what happened to my magic?

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:50.550
Looks like it failed.

00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:55.050
It was a simple Code, so it shouldn't have failed, but...

00:08:00.740 --> 00:08:01.840
Next!

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:02.930
Right!

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:12.210
Next!

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:13.840
Morishita-san!

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:16.820
Oh, right!

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:25.810
Morishita-san?

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:26.700
Hold on.

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:29.720
Class Prez, could you take Morishita-san to the infirmary?

00:08:29.720 --> 00:08:30.910
Okay.

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:35.780
I'm sorry, Prez.

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:37.490
Why are you apologizing?

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:38.530
Because...

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:43.490
Prez, be gentler with it.

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:45.650
Don't move.

00:08:45.650 --> 00:08:47.720
I'm sorry.

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:50.700
I don't understand why you'd apologize.

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:53.280
And stop calling me "Prez."

00:08:54.110 --> 00:08:55.360
I'm done.

00:08:58.490 --> 00:08:59.580
First-Aid Kit

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:06.820
Prez-I mean Kaho-chan-you live out this way?

00:09:06.820 --> 00:09:10.140
No. I'm going to Akihabara today.

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:11.800
Akihabara?

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:14.210
That's the place where, if you stand still, you end up

00:09:14.210 --> 00:09:16.150
with a bunch of guys around you taking tons of pictures!

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:20.640
Want to come with me?

00:09:31.540 --> 00:09:33.420
Would you like curry buns?

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:34.540
Sorry.

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:36.410
Could you look this way?

00:09:35.350 --> 00:09:36.420
This way please!

00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:39.740
We-We're good. We haven't been noticed yet.

00:09:39.740 --> 00:09:41.440
Morishita, you'll be left behind.

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:44.340
Huh? W-Wait up!

00:09:47.890 --> 00:09:49.920
K-Kaho-chan!

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:53.730
Wait! I'm...

00:09:57.470 --> 00:09:59.440
Parts & Repai-

00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:04.710
I forgot about Morishita.

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:12.820
We got separated.

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:36.720
I ended up someplace weird again.

00:10:44.190 --> 00:10:46.710
S-Sorry!

00:10:57.750 --> 00:11:01.050
Um... Uh...

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:03.210
Hi?

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:05.560
No!

00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:17.760
This is...

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:21.770
Damn it!

00:11:25.140 --> 00:11:30.450
I thought so. This is getting strange.

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:35.270
Oh, you're the girl from yesterday.

00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:48.970
Anehara-san, how can I ever thank you?

00:11:49.490 --> 00:11:51.440
I'm just glad she's safe.

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:54.580
Frankly, I was quite frightened.

00:11:54.580 --> 00:11:57.920
She's the lifeline of my agency.

00:11:57.920 --> 00:11:59.920
I'll tell it like it is.

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:01.980
You should stop the event.

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:06.980
My Code is having a larger effect than I thought.

00:12:06.980 --> 00:12:10.430
If you do this the wrong way, you'll create more extreme fans like we just saw.

00:12:10.430 --> 00:12:11.700
More extreme fans?

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:13.610
Well, that's absolutely perfect.

00:12:13.610 --> 00:12:16.600
It means that huge pile of money I paid you was worth it.

00:12:16.600 --> 00:12:19.080
Well, I guess I've warned you, then.

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:22.070
We've increased security. There's no problem.

00:12:22.070 --> 00:12:23.650
I see.

00:12:23.650 --> 00:12:27.140
Well, at least change out the clip I made.

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:29.820
If you want, I can put together something to replace it.

00:12:30.290 --> 00:12:32.370
Guess we have no choice.

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:40.570
You didn't copy this, did you?

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:41.950
Of course not.

00:12:41.950 --> 00:12:42.850
'Kay.

00:12:42.850 --> 00:12:44.820
I'll be contacting you later.

00:12:49.010 --> 00:12:50.670
This is perfect.

00:12:50.670 --> 00:12:52.570
You have time after this?

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:56.080
To resume our plans from yesterday.

00:13:14.260 --> 00:13:16.950
Um, what are you doing?

00:13:16.950 --> 00:13:19.510
I told you. We're finishing our activities from yesterday.

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:33.070
Here we go.

00:14:09.170 --> 00:14:10.910
Wow...

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:14.830
In the past, you might have chanted long spells

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:17.650
or undergone elaborate rituals,

00:14:18.180 --> 00:14:21.610
but recently, this is becoming more mainstream.

00:14:39.510 --> 00:14:42.340
In place of spells, you write a program to

00:14:42.340 --> 00:14:45.600
reproduce a Code on the computer.

00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:47.360
That's Modern-Day Magic.

00:14:47.780 --> 00:14:50.790
Modern-Day Magic...

00:14:52.750 --> 00:14:54.920
Work's all done.

00:14:54.920 --> 00:14:59.100
I guess all that's left is to see how well Ms. Cinderella does.

00:14:59.720 --> 00:15:03.380
When the clock strikes midnight, the magic will end.

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:28.410
Isn't that what...

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:33.740
Actually, I guess I'm impressed to see it all going as I predicted.

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:38.730
Well, then I guess I have to punish them for breaking the contract.

00:15:40.990 --> 00:15:44.010
Just what you'd expect from an Anehara Misa program.

00:15:44.010 --> 00:15:45.380
Thanks for that.

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:47.660
A-Anehara-san!

00:15:47.660 --> 00:15:50.120
I told you not to copy it.

00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:51.980
This is-

00:15:57.800 --> 00:16:00.990
All the people are leaving.

00:16:00.990 --> 00:16:03.250
The magic ended.

00:16:03.250 --> 00:16:08.770
I cast a spell that encourages purchases so people will buy her DVD.

00:16:08.770 --> 00:16:13.460
What you do is add the Charm Code to the software ahead of time.

00:16:13.460 --> 00:16:14.720
In this specific case,

00:16:14.720 --> 00:16:17.640
I added the Code to the video codec used for the promotional materials.

00:16:18.760 --> 00:16:22.380
The magic itself isn't that powerful at all,

00:16:22.380 --> 00:16:24.480
but as it's distributed on the Internet,

00:16:24.480 --> 00:16:27.000
the effect grows exponentially.

00:16:29.860 --> 00:16:33.300
But, including the Daemons from yesterday,

00:16:33.300 --> 00:16:36.780
it seems all the Codes throughout the city are acting up.

00:16:41.210 --> 00:16:46.760
Would you be interested in helping a mage on the side of good?

00:17:06.240 --> 00:17:08.180
Let go of me!

00:17:08.180 --> 00:17:10.710
No!

00:17:46.760 --> 00:17:48.990
I found the bad guy!

00:17:52.970 --> 00:17:56.720
How can you mistake your own idol,

00:17:56.720 --> 00:17:58.500
Mr. Agency President?

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:04.220
When I checked earlier, a flare was missing from your car.

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:06.040
You can't go and try to make things happen

00:18:06.040 --> 00:18:08.060
just because you want her in the news.

00:18:28.860 --> 00:18:30.280
Damn it.

00:18:30.280 --> 00:18:31.800
Damn it!

00:18:43.910 --> 00:18:47.470
I overwrote the commands on the Daemons from yesterday.

00:18:51.150 --> 00:18:52.920
D-Don't move!

00:18:54.620 --> 00:18:55.930
Where is she?

00:18:56.580 --> 00:18:58.050
Where did you hide her?!

00:18:58.050 --> 00:18:59.940
The Code's working too well, huh?

00:19:01.510 --> 00:19:04.570
I-If you don't tell me right now...

00:19:05.300 --> 00:19:06.690
It's a good luck charm.

00:19:06.690 --> 00:19:09.010
Use it if you have to.

00:19:09.010 --> 00:19:11.130
You use it the same way I taught you yesterday.

00:19:11.130 --> 00:19:13.430
But I messed that up.

00:19:13.780 --> 00:19:15.460
Can I ask you something?

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:17.380
Huh? S-Sure.

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:20.030
Why did you want to learn magic?

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:24.010
I trip over nothingness.

00:19:24.010 --> 00:19:26.420
I mess up at whatever I try.

00:19:26.420 --> 00:19:28.740
So I thought if I could use magic,

00:19:28.740 --> 00:19:31.440
maybe I could improve myself in those areas, too.

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:33.780
Magic isn't infinite.

00:19:33.780 --> 00:19:38.000
What you can do with it is limited, and learning it is extremely difficult.

00:19:39.690 --> 00:19:43.050
But as long as you don't give up,

00:19:43.050 --> 00:19:46.830
I'm sure you'll be able to find your own type of magic.

00:19:48.760 --> 00:19:51.560
My own type of magic...

00:19:50.250 --> 00:19:53.840
Damn it. You're getting in the way of our destiny together!

00:19:53.840 --> 00:19:57.270
It'll be okay. I'll be able to do it!

00:19:58.850 --> 00:20:01.240
The moment the magic completes,

00:20:01.240 --> 00:20:04.480
the Code, given form, will run throughout your body.

00:20:05.400 --> 00:20:08.640
That will be your own magic.

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:11.740
My own magic...

00:20:21.710 --> 00:20:23.520
Huh? Huh-huh?

00:20:24.600 --> 00:20:26.250
A wash basin?

00:20:26.250 --> 00:20:29.900
This is my magic?

00:20:41.410 --> 00:20:44.020
Do you really want to learn magic?

00:20:45.160 --> 00:20:48.550
I can teach you magic if you want.

00:20:48.550 --> 00:20:53.900
But I don't get much allowance, and getting a part-time job would be kind of...

00:20:53.900 --> 00:20:57.070
No, I wouldn't charge you.

00:20:57.570 --> 00:21:02.460
I'm bad using machines with more than three buttons,

00:21:02.460 --> 00:21:04.420
so will that still be okay?

00:21:04.420 --> 00:21:05.930
What are you saying?

00:21:05.930 --> 00:21:08.010
It might have been okay a hundred years ago,

00:21:08.010 --> 00:21:10.560
but computers are necessary for Modern-Day Magic.

00:21:11.030 --> 00:21:13.580
I told you it'd be hard to learn.

00:21:17.980 --> 00:21:19.600
What are you going to do?

00:21:19.600 --> 00:21:22.270
Seeing each other again today might have been by coincidence,

00:21:22.270 --> 00:21:26.440
but depending on your choice, you can change chance into fate.

00:21:39.310 --> 00:21:40.880
I'll do it!

00:21:45.880 --> 00:21:47.640
I'm Anehara Misa.

00:21:49.430 --> 00:21:51.570
Morishita Koyomi here.

00:22:06.170 --> 00:22:07.910
Morishita?

00:23:46.460 --> 00:23:48.410
The Mage Layer.

00:23:48.410 --> 00:23:52.110
It's a space where different laws take precedence.

00:23:52.110 --> 00:23:55.180
In that venue, where common sense ceases being common sense,

00:23:55.180 --> 00:23:58.170
the girl will meet another mage.

00:24:01.730 --> 00:24:06.950
Lesson 2: CDs Going on Sale

00:24:07.300 --> 00:24:11.360
The wash basin knows all! Morishita Koyomi here!

00:24:11.360 --> 00:24:14.590
I hope you enjoyed this week's episode, too. Anehara Misa here.

00:24:14.590 --> 00:24:18.720
Teacher, this week's episode didn't follow last week's.

00:24:18.720 --> 00:24:22.520
That's right. Looks like we surprised you

00:24:22.520 --> 00:24:25.310
since we didn't continue last week's story. Sorry for that.

00:24:25.310 --> 00:24:28.240
Also, next week's episode will be about how

00:24:28.240 --> 00:24:29.850
Yumiko and I meet each other in the present,

00:24:29.850 --> 00:24:32.860
unlike Episode 1 where we had met in the past.

00:24:32.860 --> 00:24:35.920
We'll air the continuation to episode 1 eventually,

00:24:35.920 --> 00:24:38.470
so be sure to wait for it, while watching the other episodes in the meantime!

00:24:38.470 --> 00:24:41.800
So, Teacher, what are we doing this week?

00:24:41.800 --> 00:24:45.640
We'll be talking about the CDs for the opening and ending!

00:24:45.150 --> 00:24:56.380
CD Details

00:24:45.640 --> 00:24:48.590
This is only episode 2, and we're doing a promotion already?

00:24:48.590 --> 00:24:50.650
Don't be all uptight!

00:24:50.650 --> 00:24:52.840
If you worry about all the little things, your hair'll fall out.

00:24:52.840 --> 00:24:54.710
I don't want that!

00:24:54.710 --> 00:24:57.000
Okay, let's begin.

00:24:57.000 --> 00:24:59.390
First up is Aso Natsuko-san's song,

00:24:59.390 --> 00:25:03.500
the opening theme for this show, "programing for non-fiction."

00:25:03.500 --> 00:25:08.360
Aso Natsuko-chan, whose popularity as an idol is suddenly increasing,

00:25:08.360 --> 00:25:11.160
likes light novels and says she read

00:25:11.160 --> 00:25:14.310
<i>Yoku Wakaru Gendai Mahou</i>

00:25:14.310 --> 00:25:18.480
and was happy to be able to sing the opening.

00:25:18.480 --> 00:25:19.710
Isn't that great?

00:25:19.710 --> 00:25:23.740
"programing for non-fiction" goes on sale 7/23.

00:25:23.740 --> 00:25:25.370
Continuing to the ending,

00:25:25.370 --> 00:25:28.520
Misato Aki-san sings "Made in WONDER."

00:25:28.520 --> 00:25:30.300
The opening's pretty cool,

00:25:30.300 --> 00:25:34.340
but the ending does a complete reversal with a happy, fun sound to it.

00:25:34.340 --> 00:25:36.690
It's wonderful that Misato-san's powerful

00:25:36.690 --> 00:25:39.980
and fun voice is synchronized to Koyomi's energetic image.

00:25:41.120 --> 00:25:44.770
"Made in WONDER" goes on sale 8/5!

00:25:44.770 --> 00:25:46.580
Both the opening and ending

00:25:46.580 --> 00:25:51.140
are great songs that add to the <i>Yoku Wakaru Gendai Mahou</i> world.

00:25:51.140 --> 00:25:53.100
Please look for them in stores.

00:25:53.100 --> 00:25:55.930
Okay! We'll end this segment

00:25:55.930 --> 00:25:58.210
watching a music clip from Aso Natsuko-san!

00:25:58.210 --> 00:25:59.410
See you next week!

00:25:59.410 --> 00:26:00.950
Bye-bye.
